{"path":"numeric/valarray/apply","title":"std::valarray<T>::apply","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::valarray&lt;T&gt;::</span>apply","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/numeric/valarray/apply","section":"numeric","kind":"page","summary":"Returns a new valarray of the same size with values which are acquired by applying function func to the previous values of the elements.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl\">\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\"> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">valarray<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> apply<span class=\"br0\">(</span> T func<span class=\"br0\">(</span>T<span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl\">\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\"> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">valarray<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> apply<span class=\"br0\">(</span> T func<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">const</span> T<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Returns a new valarray of the same size with values which are acquired by applying function <code>func</code> to the previous values of the elements.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> func\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> function to apply to the values\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p>The resulting valarray with values acquired by applying function <code>func</code>.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p>The function can be implemented with the return type different from <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/valarray\">std::valarray</a></span>. In this case, the replacement type has the following properties:\n</p>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> All <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">const</span></span> member functions of <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/valarray\">std::valarray</a></span> are provided.\n</li><li> <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/valarray\">std::valarray</a></span>, <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/valarray/slice_array\">std::slice_array</a></span>, <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/valarray/gslice_array\">std::gslice_array</a></span>, <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/valarray/mask_array\">std::mask_array</a></span> and <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/valarray/indirect_array\">std::indirect_array</a></span> can be constructed from the replacement type.\n</li><li> For every function taking a <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/valarray\"><span class=\"kw1481\">std::<span class=\"me2\">valarray</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span></span> <span class=\"t-rev-inl t-since-cxx11\"><span>except <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/valarray/begin2\"><code>begin()</code></a> and <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/valarray/end2\"><code>end()</code></a></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(since C++11)</span></span></span>, identical functions taking the replacement types shall be added;\n</li><li> For every function taking two <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/valarray\"><span class=\"kw1481\">std::<span class=\"me2\">valarray</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span></span> arguments, identical functions taking every combination of <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/valarray\"><span class=\"kw1481\">std::<span class=\"me2\">valarray</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span></span> and replacement types shall be added.\n</li><li> The return type does not add more than two levels of template nesting over the most deeply-nested argument type.\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n<h3 id=\"Possible_implementation\">Possible implementation</h3>\n<p>Following straightforward implementations can be replaced by expression templates for a higher efficiency.\n</p>\n<table class=\"eq-fun-cpp-table\">\n<tr>\n<td>\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw1\">class</span> T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span>\nvalarray<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> valarray<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">apply</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>T func<span class=\"br0\">(</span>T<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    valarray<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> other <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"sy2\">*</span>this<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"kw1\">for</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span>T<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> i <span class=\"sy4\">:</span> other<span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n        i <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> func<span class=\"br0\">(</span>i<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"kw1\">return</span> other<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw1\">class</span> T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span>\nvalarray<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> valarray<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">apply</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>T func<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">const</span> T<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    valarray<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> other <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"sy2\">*</span>this<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"kw1\">for</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span>T<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> i <span class=\"sy4\">:</span> other<span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n        i <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> func<span class=\"br0\">(</span>i<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"kw1\">return</span> other<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\"><p>Calculates and prints the first 10 factorials.</p>\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;cmath&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;iostream&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;valarray&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/valarray\"><span class=\"kw1481\">std::<span class=\"me2\">valarray</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">int</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> v <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"nu0\">1</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">2</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">3</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">4</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">5</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">6</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">7</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">8</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">9</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">10</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    v <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> v.<span class=\"me1\">apply</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">[</span><span class=\"br0\">]</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">int</span> n<span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> <span class=\"kw4\">int</span>\n                <span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n                    <span class=\"kw1\">return</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/round\"><span class=\"kw1361\">std::<span class=\"me2\">round</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/tgamma\"><span class=\"kw1357\">std::<span class=\"me2\">tgamma</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>n <span class=\"sy2\">+</span> <span class=\"nu0\">1</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n                <span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"kw1\">for</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">auto</span> n <span class=\"sy4\">:</span> v<span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n        <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> n <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">' '</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>1 2 6 24 120 720 5040 40320 362880 3628800</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/algorithm/for_each\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>for_each</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  applies a function to a range of elements <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function template)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td> <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/algorithm/ranges/for_each\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>ranges::for_each</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(C++20)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td> applies a function to a range of elements<br><span class=\"t-mark\">(algorithm function object)</span></td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Possible implementation","id":"Possible_implementation"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"numeric","title":"Numerics library"},{"path":"numeric/valarray","title":"std::valarray"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::valarray<T>::apply","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"2 declarations. Returns a new valarray of the same size with values which are acquired by applying function func to the previous…"},{"label":"Parameters","note":"func"},{"label":"Return value","note":"The resulting valarray with values acquired by applying function func."},{"label":"Notes","note":"The function can be implemented with the return type different from std::valarray."},{"label":"Possible implementation","note":"Following straightforward implementations can be replaced by expression templates for a higher efficiency."},{"label":"Example","note":"Calculates and prints the first 10 factorials."},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"for_each","note":"applies a function to a range of elements"},{"label":"ranges::for_each","note":"applies a function to a range of